{
  "_doc": "Things found while farming (scripts/systems/finds_system.gd). A family is a set of collectable kinds found by one kind of farm work. trigger.on is the work that rolls it (harvest); chance is per roll, raised by the crop's mastery stars (mastery_luck per star); pity guarantees one after that many dry rolls. Each kind has a weight (how often among its family) and a rarity. tiers are the counts owned at which the family's home grows a level; reward is paid once when every kind has been found. helps (our own touch): each find of this family adds that share to the find chance of the listed families (cap `help_cap`), so dogs sniff out gophers. trigger.when names a condition that must hold for the family to roll (queen_wanted: a Queen Bee would be of use). grant is what a find does beyond being counted (queen_bee: a Queen Bee goes to the Barn for a hive); message is a strings key that replaces the usual 'You found a ...' line.",
